VGLite — third-party notices
============================

This repository is **MIT throughout** (see LICENSE). It has no Apache-2.0 files
and no copyleft.

★ It did until 2026-08-17. The previous vendored release carried
`VGLite/vg_lite_flat.{c,h}` under Apache-2.0, and they linked into firmware --
`vg_lite.c` called their Bezier flatteners from its stroke path. The re-vendor
to MCUXpresso SDK v26.06.00-LTS (`VGLITE_HEADER_VERSION 7`) does not include
those files at all, so the exception is gone rather than corrected. This note
stays because the process that found it is the reusable part, not the finding:

  * A copyleft grep answers "is there GPL/LGPL/MPL here". It does NOT answer
    "is this repository the licence it advertises". Apache-2.0 is permissive,
    so the audit passed correctly while the README said "MIT throughout" and
    was wrong. Only a per-file survey catches that.

  * `VGLite/vg_lite_stroke.c` shipped as ISO-8859-1, and `grep -I` treats a
    non-UTF-8 file as binary and skips it silently. Measured: `grep -I` found
    nothing in it, `grep -a` found Vivante's MIT text. It was transcoded to
    UTF-8 on vendoring, and `VENDORING.md`'s re-vendoring checklist now has an
    encoding step ahead of the licence survey. A source file the sweep cannot
    read is worse than one it flags.

Both surveys are in `VENDORING.md`. Run them on every re-vendor.

Upstream provenance
-------------------

MCUXpresso SDK v26.06.00-LTS, `middleware/vglite/driver` (`mcuxsdk` commit
a910e7645d2d809a3431e1d5f42fca1cdeee69c9) — the same SDK release the sibling
